---
import VerdictChip from "../VerdictChip.astro";

/**
 * This is where the ecosystem thesis belongs — it used to be the h1, which made
 * it an essay standing where an orientation should be. Here the reader already
 * knows what Hangar is, so the thesis does the one job it is good at: it says
 * why the category has to exist at all, and it says the gap is a layering
 * decision rather than an oversight, which is the honest framing.
 *
 * The argument under it is a binary, so the section is built as one: what a
 * detector hands you on the left, what a verdict hands you on the right. The
 * header is centred; the two panels stay left-aligned inside, because lists do.
 */
import SectionHeader from "../SectionHeader.astro";
---

<section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 pb-24">
    <SectionHeader>
        Why enforcement, not detection
        <Fragment slot="lead">
            <p>
                MCP is getting a registry, tasks, and interceptors. Nothing in the protocol
                enforces anything. That's not a bug — it's a layering decision. Hangar is
                the layer.
            </p>
            <p>
                Nothing on the verdict path is scored or learned. If your platform team can
                review a NetworkPolicy, they can review a Hangar policy.
            </p>
        </Fragment>
    </SectionHeader>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-px bg-subtle rounded-3xl overflow-hidden border border-rule">
        <!-- Detection -->
        <div class="bg-ground/60 p-8 md:p-10">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-7">
                <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-rule-strong" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-ink-3 uppercase tracking-[0.16em]">Detection</span>
            </div>

            <div class="inline-flex items-baseline gap-2.5 font-mono text-base rounded-xl border border-rule bg-panel px-4 py-3 mb-7">
                <span class="text-ink-3">risk</span>
                <span class="text-ink-2 text-lg">0.87</span>
                <span class="text-ink-3">— review?</span>
            </div>

            <p class="text-lg text-ink-3 mb-7">
                A detector produces a signal, and a signal is a question. Someone has to
                triage it, decide whether it was real, and act after the fact.
            </p>
            <ul class="space-y-3.5 text-base text-ink-3">
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <span class="text-rule-strong mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true">&mdash;</span>
                    <span>Alerts you have to triage</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <span class="text-rule-strong mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true">&mdash;</span>
                    <span>Scores to tune, baselines to train</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <span class="text-rule-strong mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true">&mdash;</span>
                    <span>The call already happened</span>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Enforcement -->
        <div class="bg-subtle p-8 md:p-10 relative">
            <div
                class="absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-rule-strong to-transparent md:hidden"
                aria-hidden="true"
            ></div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-7">
                <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-ink-2" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-ink-2 uppercase tracking-[0.16em]">Enforcement</span>
            </div>

            <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2.5 font-mono text-base mb-7">
                <VerdictChip verdict="allow" />
                <span class="text-ink-3">/</span>
                <VerdictChip verdict="deny" code="isError: true" />
            </div>

            <p class="text-lg text-ink-2 mb-7">
                A policy produces a verdict, and a verdict is an answer. The tool call is
                allowed or it is not, before it reaches anything.
            </p>
            <ul class="space-y-3.5 text-base text-ink-3">
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <span class="text-rule-strong mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true">&#9654;</span>
                    <span>Admission policy on the server spec</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <span class="text-rule-strong mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true">&#9654;</span>
                    <span>Per-server egress rules and tool-schema pinning</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <span class="text-rule-strong mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true">&#9654;</span>
                    <span>Approval gates on the call path</span>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
